# Pairs with NoTrimPastLiveNeed. Issue #5417's production shape: a re-drive of a
# completed purge's tail, after its registry removal landed but the record of it
# did not, acts on the tree id without checking that the registry entry is still
# the purged tree's. Once a write has populated the id again, the re-drive trims
# the new tree's acknowledged writes and clears its pins.
MODULE: NoTrimPastLiveNeedPurgeRedriveIgnoresLineage
TARGET: NoTrimPastLiveNeed
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the purge tail's re-drive acts on a reused tree id
PERTURBS: PurgeTailRemove

--- FIND
    /\ tailOwed
    /\ tailLin = inc
--- REPLACE
    /\ tailOwed
\* MUTATION: no lineage check.
    /\ TRUE
--- END
